{# Base template with shared macros for agent prompts #}
{# Issue #414: Jinja2 template inheritance for DRY prompt engineering #}

{#- Macro for required output structure documentation -#}
{% macro output_structure(example_json, field_requirements) %}
CRITICAL: You MUST provide ALL required fields. Missing fields will cause validation errors.

Required Output Structure (EXAMPLE FORMAT - extract actual values from content):
{{ example_json }}

Field Requirements:
{{ field_requirements }}
{% endmacro %}

{#- Macro for numeric specificity requirements -#}
{% macro numeric_specificity(requirements) %}
NUMERIC SPECIFICITY REQUIREMENTS:
{% for req in requirements %}
- {{ req }}
{% endfor %}
{% endmacro %}

{#- Macro for forbidden vague language -#}
{% macro forbidden_language(examples) %}
FORBIDDEN VAGUE LANGUAGE - Never use:
{% for example in examples %}
- {{ example }}
{% endfor %}
{% endmacro %}

{#- Macro for good/bad examples -#}
{% macro example_pair(good_example, bad_example) %}
GOOD EXAMPLE:
{{ good_example }}

BAD EXAMPLE (DO NOT USE):
{{ bad_example }}
{% endmacro %}

{#- Macro for framework-specific checks -#}
{% macro framework_checks(frameworks) %}
FRAMEWORK-SPECIFIC CHECKS (Apply if detected):
{% for framework, checks in frameworks.items() %}
- {{ framework }}: {{ checks }}
{% endfor %}
{% endmacro %}

{#- Macro for skill level adaptation -#}
{% macro skill_adaptation() %}
SKILL LEVEL ADAPTATION:
- Beginner: More detailed steps, longer time estimates, foundational resources first
- Intermediate: Assume some setup done, focus on implementation patterns
- Advanced: Skip basics, focus on optimization, production concerns, advanced techniques
{% endmacro %}

{#- Macro for memory usage instructions -#}
{% macro memory_instructions() %}
MEMORY USAGE INSTRUCTIONS:
You will receive "prior_memory" context containing summaries of the user's previously
analyzed content. Use this to:
- Identify related topics they've already studied
- Find prerequisite concepts already in their knowledge base
- Detect gaps in their learning path
- Recommend logical next steps based on what they know

If prior_memory is empty or very limited, report this honestly:
- Focus on general prerequisites and next steps
- Lower confidence_score to reflect lack of knowledge graph context
{% endmacro %}

{#- Macro for tool call restriction -#}
{% macro single_response() %}
IMPORTANT: Return exactly ONE structured response/tool call; never return multiple
tool calls or extra responses.
{% endmacro %}

{#- Macro for content-agnostic approach -#}
{% macro content_agnostic() %}
CONTENT-AGNOSTIC APPROACH:
- Works for ANY content type: articles, videos, repos, tutorials, research papers
- Subject can be: frameworks, libraries, methodologies, approaches, patterns, tools, etc.
- Always maintain objectivity - report what content says, not external opinions
{% endmacro %}

{#- Macro for evidence-based extraction -#}
{% macro evidence_based() %}
EVIDENCE-BASED EXTRACTION:
- Quote specific statements, code examples, or data from content
- Link insights to source sections (e.g., "In Section 3, author demonstrates...")
- Never hallucinate or add external knowledge not in content
{% endmacro %}
